                    },
                    "message": "Let me get on that."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.cpp",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm fine with doing that."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "this needs documentation probably, and elsewhere"
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, can we get some doxygen here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Do we have a requirement somewhere that we use doxygen format?  I agree, this could use some comments for a description, but adding doxygen everywhere seems like a mess for something I'm not aware we use."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "It was mean as a short hand for documenting the interfaces in doxygen/javadocs style. I don\u2019t care about the tools themselves but it\u2019s pretty standard way to document C++ and widely used in openbmc, yes."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "If it's ok, I'd like to not hold up this refactor on that.  I added these methods originally, I can go clean them up if we're going to require doxygen.\n\nsdbusplus doesn't use doxygen anywhere, does it?  stdplus doesn't that I can see.  libcper/libpldm doesn't.  What common library does openbmc use do a good job of doxygen strings?  I'm happy to start with platform-init, I'm just a little surprised at the request."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Sorry, this was slightly wrong, libpldm does in fact do doxygen."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "sdbusplus also does.  It even generates doxygen for the bindings it creates, from the YAML definitions.\n\nMany of our non-library [application] repositories also do.\n\n```\n$ rg \"@param\" -t cpp -l | sed \"s#/.*##\" | sort | uniq | gh gist create          \n- Creating gist...\n\u2713 Created secret gist\n```\nhttps://gist.github.com/williamspatrick/e0ffb79138f36beea51dd1c834b9b2d0"
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Yep... right you are.  I was looking at a file that didn't have docs.  I'll get them added at the top of this series."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.hpp",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there any reason why this is better than just using libgpiod-cxx directly?  It isn't clear to me..."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.hpp",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This one adds logging.  Might not be needed other than that."
                },
                {
                    "file": "gpio.hpp",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "i2c.cpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "How do we plan to handle two different DC-SCM in the same server: Aspeed-2600 and Aspeed-2700 (as examples)?  The bus numbers could change between the two BMC chips."
                },
                {
                    "file": "i2c.cpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "There was some back and forth on this on Ed's patch. The idea was to change this to be a bus number rather than this crappy string, and keep a map internally to this function. We could expand that to do a check internally based on the SoC (we should be able to get that from the filesystem somewhere, or from a reg in the absolute worst case). I'm not sold on this idea, just a thought. I do (in a future patch), want to get rid of this hacky string passing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "i2c.cpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "i2c.hpp",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "no tabs. Also will follow up with stronger typing in a followup review."
                },
                {
                    "file": "i2c.hpp",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform.cpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I really liked how you could read the old one like a sentence.  Oh well, I guess this is progress."
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform.cpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "I guess I don't really care other than gpio::set_gpio feels silly. And setting a precedent of \"no namespaces\" seems silly at the start of a project."
                },
                {
                    "file": "utilities.cpp",
                    "line": 34,
